          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "2. The Nice-Slice Argument",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            318.07,
            241.71,
            330.03
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMBX10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Consider the process by which a collection of particles of total mass M gravitation-",
          "bbox": [
            95.88,
            347.91,
            540.28,
            359.87
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "ally collapses to form a black hole. In the absence of any net angular momentum, the",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            368.31,
            540.05,
            380.27
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "black hole becomes approximately spherically symmetric in a short time after the collapse",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            388.71,
            540.04,
            400.67
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "process. As long as we are only considering processes with lifetimes short compared to",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            409.11,
            539.97,
            421.07
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "G2M 3, we can approximate the geometry of the system by the Schwarzschild solution.",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            427.88,
            540.1,
            441.47
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "CMR7"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            8.37,
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The nice-slice argument begins by introducing a family of Cauchy surfaces which foliate",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            449.91,
            540.17,
            461.87
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "the geometry. The surfaces should avoid regions of strong spacetime curvature and yet",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            470.31,
            539.98,
            482.27
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "cut through the infalling matter and the outgoing Hawking radiation so that both sets of",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            490.71,
            540.07,
            502.67
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "particles have low energy in the local frame of the slice. Also, in order to ensure that short",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            511.11,
            540.0,
            523.07
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "distance physics does not creep in to the description through the choice of coordinates, we",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            531.51,
            540.04,
            543.47
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "require that the slices be everywhere smooth, with small extrinsic curvature compared to",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            551.91,
            539.99,
            563.87
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "any microscopic scale. For convenience, we will choose surfaces that agree with surfaces",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            572.31,
            539.78,
            584.27
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "of constant Schwarzschild time far from the black hole. Such a family of surfaces will",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            592.71,
            540.1,
            604.67
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "henceforth be designated “nice slices”. While it is seldom spelled out, the existence of",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            613.11,
            540.06,
            625.07
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "such a set of surfaces is implicitly assumed in much of the existing literature on black hole",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            633.51,
            540.06,
            645.47
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "evaporation. The ﬁrst explicit construction of nice slices that we are aware of was carried",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            653.91,
            540.04,
            665.87
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "out by Wald [13].",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            674.31,
            163.19,
            686.27
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To construct an example of a family of nice slices, we begin with the Schwarzschild",
          "bbox": [
            95.88,
            695.43,
            539.7,
            707.39
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "black hole in Kruskal-Szekeres coordinates, as shown in ﬁg. 1. These coordinates are related",
          "bbox": [
            72.0,
            715.83,
            540.03,
            727.79
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
